# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers.
#
# This file is the ONLY place they can land for the web app. The SPA has two
# publishers, and both serve this file: Cloudflare Pages
# (`wrangler pages deploy dist` in .github/workflows/deploy-claxedo-app.yml) and
# the user deployment's static-assets Worker
# (packages/claxedo-server/scripts/deploy/deploy-user-cloudflare.ts). Neither
# routes the HTML document through the control-plane Worker, so the Hono
# `securityHeaders()` middleware in
# packages/claxedo-server/src/deployments/hosted-shared/hosted-core-app.ts
# covers the API responses and NOTHING here. Both surfaces need their own set.
#
# A Cache-Control set here replaces the publisher's default
# (`public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`) rather than adding to it, and a second
# matching rule that sets any header again is joined to the first with a comma.
# Everything outside /assets carries `no-transform`: the SPA shell is the only
# HTML either publisher serves, and Cloudflare's HTML features (email
# obfuscation, Rocket Loader, injected beacons) would add inline scripts the
# build's meta Content-Security-Policy refuses. The directive also stops
# Cloudflare compressing those responses, which costs about 3 KB on the shell.
# The rest of the value is the default revalidation the shell, its client routes
# (/, /w/:id, /s/:id) and unhashed root files need, so a new deploy's asset
# references are picked up at once.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-transform, public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Both publishers serve this project over HTTPS only, so the HSTS pin is
  # unconditional here. (The control plane's HSTS is gated on transport because
  # it also runs plaintext on localhost; the app's publishers never do.) No `preload` — that is a
  # one-way door that needs a deliberate submission, not a config default.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  # Legacy clickjacking header, kept for pre-CSP2 browsers only. Every current
  # browser IGNORES it when `frame-ancestors` is present, and frame-ancestors
  # below is authoritative. SAMEORIGIN matches the frame-ancestors policy on
  # old browsers.
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  # The fetch directives are enforced by the build's <meta http-equiv> policy
  # (vite.web-document.ts), which names the exact server and relay
  # origins. A meta policy cannot carry frame-ancestors, so it stays here.
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'

# Vite writes only content-hashed scripts, styles and media under /assets (e.g.
# main-DUtf99h4.js), so they are immutable. Both publishers apply a rule's `!`
# detach before its own values, so this value replaces the one above instead of
# being joined to it. Without `no-transform` Cloudflare compresses them, which
# takes main-*.js from 3.6 MB to about 1.0 MB. Content-Type is left to the
# publisher, which derives it from the extension; a rule here would be joined to
# any other matching Content-Type rule and name no type Cloudflare compresses.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
